    "deepTech": "Each PVT corner stresses a different physical failure mechanism: Hot + Low Voltage (e.g., 85–105 °C, Vmin): Cell capacitor leakage increases exponentially with temperature (requiring faster tREFI refresh), while slow silicon + low voltage degrade slew rate and setup margin—causing bit flips, Synchronous External abort, or SError. Cold (e.g., −10 °C to −25 °C): Interconnect/transistor characteristics shift sharply; as observed in my Google thermal-to-silicon investigation, extreme cold (−25.56 °C chamber / −8 °C die) can drive ZQCal FSMs to saturate at 0x1ff, collapsing impedance matching and triggering GMC/GSLC interrupts (0x400/0x100) at PF State 13. Dynamic DVFS Transitions: Stepping between PF states stresses PMIC settling and PLL/PHY re-locking.",
