    "deepTech": "Random crashes usually fall into four buckets: (1) Power/Brownout (PMIC UVLO or dI/dt droop causing silent hard reset with zero OS kernel panic); (2) Thermal runaway/throttling; (3) Memory/Cache corruption (MCE, SError, ECC DBE); or (4) PCIe/Driver deadlock (AER Fatal, GPU Xid 79 fallen off bus). Knowing whether the OS printed a panic/Xid vs died instantly without a single UART byte immediately splits hardware power/reset faults from software/bus faults.",
