    "deepTech": "Thermal throttling happens when junction or board temperatures exceed firmware thresholds, causing clocks and voltage to step down to protect silicon—which can masquerade as a performance regression or intermittent timing failure. In my Google bench work, I also saw how host-level or chamber-level sensors can differ significantly from on-die silicon sensors, so correlating sensors / nvidia-smi die temps with bench airflow/chiller state prevents misdiagnosing a cooling failure as bad silicon.",
