    "deepTech": "Cold power-on, warm reset, and sleep-resume leave completely different amounts of residual state inside the memory controller, PHY PLLs, and DRAM mode registers, so they must never be conflated. Likewise, combining cleaning, reseating, firmware changes, and voltage margining in a single step makes it impossible to know which action actually cured the symptom.",
