    "deepTech": "A common trap is guessing what 0,8,10,16 mean without checking the firmware's pattern table—they are stimulus pattern IDs, not voltage states. Isolating which pattern fails guides physical debug: checkerboard exposes adjacent-line crosstalk/coupling, solid 1s/0s expose DC power droop or stuck faults, and address patterns expose decode/aliasing issues. Likewise, you must verify actual rank/cache mapping before claiming full DRAM coverage.",
