    "sectionTitle": "Communication & Boundaries (Q1–Q5)",
    "q": "Comm Q2: Tell me about a time your attention to detail caught a subtle hardware or test issue.",
    "whatISay": "During DRAM DVFS validation at Google, an automated summary flagged two failures at cold temperature, and initial assumptions pointed to a bad DRAM die or chamber threshold. Looking closely at the raw target logs, I noticed two details: first, Loop 1 aborted in 5 seconds due to unwanted GMC and GSLC interrupts rather than finishing 50 loops; second, the appended chamber temperature (-25.6°C) didn't match the on-die sensors (-8°C memss, -3°C aoc) because of run-boundary logging offsets. Separating those facts prevented a false root-cause conclusion and focused debug on the exact PF13 interrupt and ZQCal state.",
