    "deepTech": "For example, if tRAS = 32 ns and tRP = 14 ns, then tRC must be at least 46 ns (exact numbers come from the JEDEC/device datasheet for the active speed bin). Violating tRAS cuts off charge restoration before the cell reaches full voltage, causing weak-cell read failures later; violating tRP leaves bitlines unequally precharged, shrinking sensing margin on the next ACTIVATE.",
