      "Step 2 (Verify remote sense & protection resistors): Confirm 10–100 Ω sense-safety resistors exist across force/sense lines so if a Kelvin sense wire pops loose, the PSU does not slew to OVP max!",
      "Step 3 (Confirm sense polarity): Never accidentally swap +Sense and -Sense; negative feedback turns positive and slams output voltage to supply ceiling.",
      "Step 4 (Configure PSU limits): Program hardware OVP (Over-Voltage Protection) just above Vmax (e.g. Vnom + 10%) and start current limit safely low for initial boot check.",
      "Step 5 (Check cooling & airflow before enable): Even idle boot leakage on a multi-hundred-watt silicon die heats up to >100 C within seconds without seated TIM + thermal head.",
      "Step 6 (Ramp & inspect): Toggle output while monitoring scope PG/ramp monotonicity and current draw before launching full stress."
