    "lesson": "Bootstrap resistors set external hardware choices (boot device, reference clock freq, debug enable) latched ONLY during reset edge (so multi-function pins become GPIO/UART right after reset!); OTP eFuses burn silicon permanently (ECID, repair redundancy, security keys, SKU enable) and typically lock out external strap overrides once blown.",
