      "Step 2 (Classic board bug on shared straps): Connecting an unbuffered strong push-pull peripheral (say UART-USB adapter or pull-down PHY!) onto a strapping pin steals voltage away from the 4.7 kΩ strap resistor and silently flips `BOOT_MODE` into dead DFU/recovery mode!",
      "Step 3 (Define OTP eFuses): Polysilicon/metal electromigration fuses burned permanently at wafer probe/FT—storing unique die `ECID`, SRAM row/column repair addresses, speed-bin trim, SKU core counts, and secure-boot public key hash.",
      "Step 4 (Security priority): On production (\"fused/PROD\") parts, security eFuses override external debug straps so an attacker cannot simply solder a pull-up resistor onto `JTAG_EN` to read encrypted keys!",
