      "Step 2 (Culprit #1 — `WP# / IO2` or `HOLD# / IO3` board resistors!): Many reference designs tie `WP#` or `HOLD#` to a pull-up/strap or test jumper—if held hard by a low resistor or capacitor on `IO2`/`IO3`, Quad bits freeze at 0 or 1!",
