      "Step 2 (Compare EEPROM vs BMC): Dumb EEPROMs never clock-stretch; MCUs/BMCs stretch whenever their CPU gets stalled in higher-priority interrupts or flash writes.",
      "Step 3 (Identify the two failure modes): (a) Host I2C peripheral honors SMBus `t_LOW:SEXT` / timeout (~25–35 ms), drops `STOP`, and fails transaction (`-ETIMEDOUT` / `0xFF`), OR (b) Misconfigured push-pull host clock driver fights the BMC holding `SCL` LOW (mid-rail glitch!).",
