    "visualParams": {
      "highlight": "Common 100 MHz REFCLK vs SRIS Elastic Buffer",
      "fault": "Clock Domain Buffer Slip"
    },
    "lesson": "Common-Clock drives BOTH Root Complex and Endpoint from the SAME 100 MHz motherboard/riser clock (meaning zero long-term frequency ppm offset—just small constant phase skew!). SRIS runs completely independent crystals PLUS up to `-0.5%` (5,000 ppm) down-spread SSC -> total differential slip reaches **5,600 ppm**, overflowing normal small Common-Clock RX elastic buffers constantly unless both sides enable wide SRIS elastic buffers + dense SKP cadence!",
    "formula": "Common Clk Δf = 0 ppm ; SRNS Δf <= 600 ppm ; SRIS Δf <= 5600 ppm!",
    "sub": "",
    "unit": "concept",
    "unitConv": "Explain with exact SI/EE units, physical mechanism, and bench verification step.",
    "steps": [
      "Step 1 (Common-Clock — Gold standard on boards/slots): One 100 MHz generator fans out cleanly via PCIe slot pin `REFCLK+/REFCLK-` to Endpoint GPU AND Root Complex! Even if SSC swings -0.5% down, BOTH ends rise/fall together -> ~0 ppm net average frequency offset!",
      "Step 2 (SRNS — Separate Refclk No SSC): Long optical/cabled risers omit carrying 100 MHz REFCLK in cables; each box uses an independent ±300 ppm crystal (`<= 600 ppm` total max delta, SSC MUST stay OFF!).",
      "Step 3 (SRIS — Separate Refclk Independent SSC): Independent clocks BOTH allowed to turn -0.5% (5,000 ppm) triangular SSC ON independently -> one end runs slow (-5000 - 300 ppm) while other stays peak (+300 ppm) = **5,600 ppm mismatch**!",
      "Step 4 (Hardware Elastic Buffer impact): RX writes data with recovered TX clock and reads out with local clock; at 5,600 ppm, FIFO fills/drains ~9x faster than SRNS and requires larger depth + denser `SKP` ordered-set frequency!",
      "Step 5 (Classic SLT Bench Bring-Up Bug!): Plugging an independent-oscillator PCIe adapter or test bench REFCLK generator into a motherboard running SSC without enabling SRIS in BIOS & GPU config causes periodic `RX Elastic Buffer Overflow/Underflow` AER errors every few microseconds!",
      "Step 6 (Quick bench check): Probe Root `REFCLK` vs Endpoint `REFCLK` simultaneously OR turn SSC OFF cleanly on clock gen to confirm whether errors drop immediately to 0!"
    ],
