    "lesson": "**#1 Hardware Destruction Rule:** NEVER probe a DC voltage/power rail directly into a Spectrum Analyzer’s bare `50 Ω` RF input without an external high-voltage **DC-Block capacitor + series attenuator** (`0 V DC max` mixers fry instantaneously at 3.3 V/12 V!). Meanwhile, narrowing `RBW` (`e.g. 100 kHz -> 1 kHz`) drops the analyzer noise floor 20 dB and cleanly separates close sideband switching spurs from the carrier skirt!",
