      "Step 2 (Choose `H-field Loop` vs `E-field Stub` probe): `H-field loop` detects magnetic switching current loops (`VRM inductors`, `high-di/dt caps`, `return splits`); rotate loop 90° to pinpoint magnetic field direction (`max when plane aligns with current trace!`). `E-field tip` finds noisy high-voltage switching pads (`SW nodes`, `unshielded clocks`).",
      "Step 3 (Configure `Span` & `Center Freq`): Center `100 MHz`, Span `5 MHz` to hunt close `±500 kHz..2 MHz` VRM switching sidebands around REFCLK.",
