      "Step 2 (Culprit #1 — **Wrong Device Tree Trigger Polarity / Level vs Edge**): Suppose PMIC asserts active-LOW fault (`0 V` fault, `1.8 V` normal), yet Linux DT configures `IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH` (`4`): while line sits completely normal idle HIGH at `1.8 V`, kernel fires continuously at max speed!",
      "Step 3 (Culprit #2 — **Floating / Un-Pulled Open-Drain `INT#` Pin**): Missing pull-up leaves active-LOW `INT#` floating near `0 V` constantly!",
      "Step 4 (Culprit #3 — **Missing Hardware Status Clear Inside ISR / Shared Interrupt**): Level-triggered handler reads wrong status offset (`W1C write-1-to-clear bit not cleared`), returning cleanly while peripheral still holds pin LOW -> instant re-trigger!",
      "Step 5 (Isolate cleanly on bench): Probe that physical `INT#` pin voltage on scope (`sitting flat LOW/HIGH vs real rapid pulsing?`), and inspect DT `interrupts = <pin IRQ_TYPE_...>` definition.",
