    "lesson": "`devmem2` maps physical `/dev/mem` via `mmap(..., O_SYNC)` so CPU reads uncached single-beat load/store directly onto AXI/APB! Three instant crashes: (1) reading/writing an **unclocked or power-gated** IP block (instant AXI hang / SError!); (2) **wrong access width / alignment** (`8-bit/16-bit` read on strictly `32-bit`-only APB slave -> Bus Error!); and (3) stepping directly on registers actively owned/cached by running kernel drivers (`race corruption`)!",
