    "unitConv": "Explain with exact SI/EE units, physical mechanism, and bench verification step.",
    "steps": [
      "Step 1 (Don’t power-cycle blindly—preserve Root & Switch & GPU telemetry!): Disable instant auto-reboot (`panic=0`) or examine `EDAC/MCE/AER` decoded `dmesg` + BMC SEL logs + standby I2C GPU sideband (`SMBPBI` / JTAG)!",
      "Step 2 (Read exact MCE / AER signature): Confirm `AER Completion Timeout` (`bit 14 UESta`) AND check whether `Surprise Down` / `Surprise Link Error` (`LTSSM` dropped completely!) accompanied `CTO` vs link stayed in clean `L0`!",
      "Step 3 (Split Wire Drop vs Internal GPU Hang!): If `LTSSM == L0` cleanly with `0` `BadDLLP/RxErr` AND ONLY that read timed out -> GPU received `MRd` cleanly at PCIe core, forwarded it inside GPU NoC/MMIO, and **internal GPU core stalled/forgot to answer**! Whereas massive `RxErr/BadDLLP + Surprise Down` means physical SerDes link broke!",
      "Step 4 (Check Device Power State at crash instant!): Was runtime PM (`D3cold` / `RTD3` power-down!) turning GPU off just as another driver/cron/prometheus exporter tried reading `/sys/...` MMIO (`un-woken D3 read = classic CTO!`)?",
      "Step 5 (Check GPU Internal Crash Flags via Sideband I2C / JTAG!): Read sticky GPU fault status, `PMIC STATUS` (`did GPU core VRM silently trip OC and drop out mid-read?!`), and GPU thermal state over out-of-band BMC/I2C!",
      "Step 6 (Trace exact offending MMIO Offset using `ftrace / driver instrumentation`): Set PCIe Protocol Analyzer on the slot triggered cleanly on `CTO / >1 ms unanswered ReqID+Tag` to print exact `BAR Address Offset`!",
      "Step 7 (Test isolating variables): Turn OFF runtime power management (`power/control=on`), cap PCIe speed down cleanly to `Gen3`, and run failing test again.",
      "Step 8 (Deliver crystal-clear triage packet!): Separate (A) Link drop -> SI/socket, (B) VRM dropout -> PDN/PMIC, (C) D3 race -> Kernel driver fix, or (D) Specific BAR Offset internal hang -> Silicon RTL/FW bug!"
    ],
