    "lesson": "`line.split()[4]` shatters the moment a log adds a space or negative sign (`-10.5C` vs ` 25.0C`), and greedy `.*` grabs across multiple columns on one line! Use **compiled named regex groups** (`re.compile(r\"Tj=(?P<tj>[-+]?d+(?:.d+)?)C.*Vdd=(?P<vdd>d+)mV\")`), non-greedy qualifiers (`.*?`), word boundaries (`\b`), and explicit `None`-checked casting (`int(m[\"ecid\"], 16)`).",
