      "Step 2 (Set exact byte order & format cleanly over SCPI): Send `:WAV:FORM WORD; :WAV:BYT LSBF` (`little-endian`, matching x86 NumPy `<i2`) + read `:WAV:PRE?` preamble header BEFORE fetching bulk waveform!",
      "Step 3 (Decode IEEE 488.2 Arbitrary Block Header `#<d><N>` manually or via PyVISA `query_binary_values`): First char `#`, next 1 ASCII digit `d` (`e.g. \"8\"`), next `d` chars give exact binary payload byte length `N` (`\"020000000\"` bytes), followed by trailing `\n` terminator (`verify you strip trailing \n cleanly!`!).",
      "Step 4 (Check PyVISA shortcut AND Endianness!): `inst.query_binary_values(\":WAV:DATA?\", datatype=\"h\", is_big_endian=False, container=np.ndarray)` handles block header length automatically cleanly into NumPy!",
