    "question": "A healthy Fast-Process wafer lot shifts mean `IDDQ` up by `+40%` (`well inside electrical spec!`) causing a rigid **Static `IDDQ` Limit** to scrap **18% of the wafer**—meanwhile slow wafers with low `IDDQ` let real `+3x` defect outliers sneak right under the loose static ceiling! How does **Dynamic Part Average Testing (`DPAT`)** solve BOTH problems cleanly?",
