    "kind": "concept",
    "question": "You wire a JTAG debugger onto a fresh prototype SLT board and attempt to read GPU **`IDCODE`**. Case A prints **`0xFFFFFFFF`**, Case B prints **`0x00000000`**, and Case C prints **garbage alternating hex (`e.g. 0x9F2A...`) that shifts randomly per run**! Decode all three physical JTAG faults cleanly.",
    "visualKind": "soc-blocks",
