    "modelAnswer": "In IEEE 1149.1 JTAG: **`0xFFFFFFFF`** means open/un-driven `TDO` (`pull-up reads 1` -> check `VDD_JTAG`, active-low `TRST#`, debugger `VREF`, broken daisy-chain jumper); **`0x00000000`** means `TDO` pulled dead LOW (`GND short` or unpowered chip clamping `TDO` through ESD diode); and **changing/shifted garbage** indicates `TCK` edge reflections double-clocking the TAP FSM (`verify by dropping TCK down to 100 kHz and scoping TCK monotonicity`)."
