    "question": "Firmware release **`v1.2`** passed 100% last Monday; today **`v1.3` (`containing 128 commits across VBIOS, PMIC tables, Linux driver, and Python scripts`)** fails `20%` on PCIe! Explain how you isolate the exact breaking commit (`plus watch out for intermittent `20%` repro flakiness during bisection!`!) in **~7 runs cleanly**.",
